ry the brace for two weeks and see how your knee feels? If it does not help, we will talk about alternatives. And the exercise we prescribe will not be \'stop moving\' — it will be smarter, more targeted exercise that protects your muscles instead of burning them out.\'\n\n**6. Normalize the emotional response**:\n\'Many polio survivors feel exactly the way you do when they hear this diagnosis. There is a grief in confronting this after so many years of doing well. If you are open to it, I can connect you with a support group of other polio survivors going through the same thing. Sometimes talking to someone who truly understands your experience can help.\'\n\n**Key principles demonstrated**: Respecting patient identity and autonomy, reframing medical reality without dismissing emotions, using relatable analogies, motivational interviewing approach, collaborative goal-setting, graduated acceptance, peer support referral.',
